1
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:05,980
=The Cruel Tribunal=
=Episode 14=

2
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,600
Who was it back then

3
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,320
who ordered you
to administer the poison?

4
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:13,360
Speak!

5
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,400
Who was it?

6
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:19,960
Empress...

7
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:21,760
Empress Jingshu.

8
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:31,040
From today onward,

9
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,680
you'll do

10
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:35,800
whatever I tell you.

11
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:37,040
Yes.

12
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:40,560
Your wife and son

13
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:44,400
will be safe.

14
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:46,800
Thank you, sir.

15
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,280
Thank you, sir.

16
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,640
Thank you, sir.

17
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:51,280
Thank you, sir.

18
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:54,720
Thank you, sir.

19
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:00,800
Don't worry.

20
00:02:01,520 --> 00:02:03,160
Once the job is done,

21
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:06,800
Ma Shuan will return home safely.

22
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:14,680
But please remember,

23
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:18,040
don't say anything

24
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:20,040
you shouldn't.

25
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:21,000
Understand?

26
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:22,600
Rest assured, sir.

27
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,240
We won't say a word.

28
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,720
Pardon us.

29
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:32,080
You can go now.

30
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:34,600
Hurry!

31
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:36,320
Come on.

32
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:37,480
Go.

33
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:38,120
I'm not going!

34
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:38,640
Hurry!

35
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:39,640
I want my father!

36
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:40,480
Hurry!

37
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:41,560
I'm not going!

38
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:42,520
Get out!

39
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:44,720
Go!

40
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:50,280
Thank you, sir.

41
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,480
Thank you, sir.

42
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:52,800
Thank you, sir.

43
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:53,600
Thank...

44
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:57,160
Thank you, sir.

45
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:14,740
(Spirit Tablet of My Mother, Yanshu)

46
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:22,480
Mother.

47
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:23,160
Who are you?

48
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,120
What do you want?

49
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:28,160
(I will avenge my mother's murder)

50
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:30,280
(in this lifetime.)

51
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:37,560
Mother,

52
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,160
I've come to pay my respects.

53
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:41,840
Piao, what brings you here at this hour?

54
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:44,640
I heard

55
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:46,520
you've been so worried

56
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,560
about Father's health

57
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:49,520
that you've fallen ill yourself.

58
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,760
So I came especially to see you.

59
00:03:52,320 --> 00:03:53,040
My child,

60
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:54,040
how thoughtful of you.

61
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:58,980
Please wait a moment, Mother.

62
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:09,960
This cat

63
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,440
is truly quite strange.

64
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:13,120
No matter how much you feed it,

65
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,360
it always seems

66
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,600
to pretend to seek your affection.

67
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,760
Yet it isn't afraid of people.

68
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,360
When someone approaches,

69
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:21,760
it doesn't make a fuss.

70
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:28,640
Keeping its distance
like this would be one thing,

71
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:31,120
but without warning,
it may even scratch you.

72
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:32,920
Hearing you say that, Mother,

73
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:35,720
don't you think people are the same?

74
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:38,080
Some people

75
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:39,680
are impossible to read,

76
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:41,160
impossible to win over,

77
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:44,480
and may suddenly

78
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,360
turn on you.

79
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:49,840
Piao,

80
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:51,920
what you say

81
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:53,360
does make some sense.

82
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:55,960
Come.

83
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,560
Sit and talk with me.

84
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:07,080
Then do you think

85
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:08,360
acting this way

86
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,600
is wrong?

87
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:12,600
Wrong?

88
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,840
Take your father, for example.

89
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:16,840
When he speaks to his ministers,

90
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:20,040
there's always another meaning
behind his words.

91
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,960
You may see him at morning court

92
00:05:22,960 --> 00:05:25,200
praising someone
for their loyalty and dedication,

93
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:27,000
but in truth,

94
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,280
the very next day,
he may dismiss and investigate them.

95
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,560
The art of ruling

96
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,160
is about

97
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:35,920
balancing power

98
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:37,680
and influence,

99
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:40,200
not

100
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,760
personal feelings.

101
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,240
Sometimes,

102
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:46,200
even with me,

103
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:48,320
he keeps certain things to himself.

104
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:50,400
Then do you think

105
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:52,160
what your father does

106
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:53,400
is right

107
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:54,680
or wrong?

108
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:56,800
I believe

109
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:00,080
that given Father's position,

110
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:03,560
there is simply
no question of right or wrong,

111
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:07,320
nor does he need
to justify himself to anyone.

112
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:10,800
Even if Father is wrong,

113
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,880
he must still be right,

114
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:18,680
because he is
the one pillar holding together

115
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:21,440
the entire court

116
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:23,880
and even the whole of Bojue Kingdom.

117
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:32,400
He's like the main beam
of this great hall.

118
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,480
No matter how fierce the storm,

119
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:38,040
he must hold firm.

120
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:42,600
The moment Father begins to doubt

121
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:45,000
what he has done,

122
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,320
or hesitate,

123
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:49,400
it would be like this main beam.

124
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:52,160
Even the slightest sway

125
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:54,960
would bring

126
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:57,520
the entire building down.

127
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:02,880
Is that so?

128
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:05,600
Then, Piao,

129
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,200
when you inherit the throne one day,

130
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:09,240
will you be the same?

131
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:11,080
Always right,

132
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:12,520
never wrong.

133
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:19,440
I

134
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:22,440
certainly will.

135
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:29,320
Piao,

136
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:33,040
having you here to talk with me today

137
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,120
has eased

138
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:35,720
some of my worries.

139
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:38,000
It's getting late.

140
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:39,880
You should go back and rest.

141
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:43,880
Yes.

142
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:55,040
I'll take my leave.

143
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:06,560
(Mother.)

144
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,440
(Jingshu cannot die.)

145
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:11,040
(Only she truly understands me.)

146
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:14,520
(Only she can help me claim the realm.)

147
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:18,060
(Archives Repository)

148
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,040
From now on,

149
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,040
the laws of our dynasty

150
00:08:20,050 --> 00:08:22,800
shall uphold the principle of legality
as their foremost principle.

151
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:24,200
Crimes and punishments

152
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,840
must be expressly prescribed by law.

153
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:27,520
No local official

154
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:29,920
may create new crimes
or punishments without authorization.

155
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:32,760
But,

156
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:34,440
with such a rule,

157
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,960
what if someone commits a heinous act

158
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:38,840
that is not

159
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:40,120
covered by our laws?

160
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:41,280
Wouldn't that

161
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:43,400
allow the offender to escape punishment?

162
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:44,600
Chief Clerk,

163
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,120
do you believe

164
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,680
there could ever be a law

165
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:49,840
that covers every crime
that exists today

166
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:51,590
while also anticipating
those of the future?

167
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,310
I've never heard of such a thing.

168
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:55,920
Exactly.

169
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:58,200
If, merely because
of such unforeseen cases,

170
00:08:58,280 --> 00:08:59,800
we give local officials

171
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:01,280
the power to create crimes at will,

172
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:02,520
wouldn't that...

173
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:05,760
Forgive my ignorance.

174
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:07,880
The core of the principle of legality

175
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:09,720
is to curb the abuse of public power.

176
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,520
Loopholes in the law can be remedied,

177
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:12,990
but its limits
must never be overstepped.

178
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:14,960
A wise decision.

179
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,640
Bind these into volumes first.

180
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:18,960
I'll take them to Her Highness.

181
00:09:19,460 --> 00:09:20,000
- Yes.
- Yes.

182
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:34,040
(Why is Sizhou here too?)

183
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:36,920
The First Prince has arrived.

184
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:39,680
Greetings, Mother.

185
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:41,440
Have a seat.

186
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:44,800
Zhou,

187
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:46,720
how is your injury?

188
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,080
I've fully recovered.

189
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:49,470
Thank you for your concern, Mother.

190
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:50,640
I'm glad you're safe.

191
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:52,040
I'm glad you're safe.

192
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:54,400
Your uncle, Prince Luan, and I

193
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:55,990
have been worried
about you all this time.

194
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:58,120
We've been hoping you'd return soon.

195
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:58,680
Yes.

196
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,280
I was just about to go and thank Uncle.

197
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:02,440
During this campaign,

198
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:04,600
the provisions, weapons,
and overall coordination

199
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,560
could never have gone so smoothly
without Uncle's efforts.

200
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:07,360
Zhou,

201
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:10,360
your uncle and I
have already discussed it.

202
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:11,640
Before long,

203
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:12,800
we'll choose an auspicious day

204
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,360
and grant you marriage

205
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:15,600
to Rousang.

206
00:10:22,470 --> 00:10:25,070
♪The candle burns down
to its final glow♪

207
00:10:26,030 --> 00:10:28,430
♪Cold fragrance clings to my hem♪

208
00:10:29,070 --> 00:10:30,830
♪You gently smooth my hair♪

209
00:10:30,830 --> 00:10:33,750
♪Yet your gaze drifts far away♪

210
00:10:36,190 --> 00:10:38,630
♪A hidden blade lies beneath your smile♪

211
00:10:38,990 --> 00:10:42,310
♪You turn away
as if nothing has changed♪

212
00:10:42,910 --> 00:10:44,470
♪Step by step, I walk away♪

213
00:10:44,630 --> 00:10:47,950
♪Each step breaks my heart anew♪

214
00:10:50,710 --> 00:10:53,590
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

215
00:10:54,110 --> 00:10:57,190
♪Why leave me
standing alone in the wind?♪

216
00:10:57,630 --> 00:11:00,230
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

217
00:11:00,230 --> 00:11:04,270
♪Yet all that's left
is warmth upon my fingertips♪

218
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:07,550
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

219
00:11:07,950 --> 00:11:10,630
♪And write of every meeting
and every parting♪

220
00:11:10,630 --> 00:11:13,350
♪If next life asks
about the days gone by♪

221
00:11:13,630 --> 00:11:16,590
♪I'll only say that once♪

222
00:11:17,070 --> 00:11:18,830
♪I called your name♪

223
00:11:23,430 --> 00:11:25,670
♪The silent stars hang low♪

224
00:11:27,070 --> 00:11:29,270
♪The river keeps flowing east♪

225
00:11:30,510 --> 00:11:32,430
♪I linger in the old tower♪

226
00:11:32,550 --> 00:11:36,190
♪Waiting for you,
though all is now empty♪

227
00:11:37,510 --> 00:11:39,950
♪This life still owes us a bow♪

228
00:11:40,830 --> 00:11:43,630
♪May the next repay us with a dream♪

229
00:11:44,390 --> 00:11:46,630
♪Beyond here lie
endless mountains and rivers♪

230
00:11:46,630 --> 00:11:52,870
♪I dare not turn for one last look♪

231
00:11:53,150 --> 00:11:56,030
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

232
00:11:56,630 --> 00:12:00,110
♪Why bury this heart beneath the frost?♪

233
00:12:00,110 --> 00:12:02,750
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

234
00:12:02,750 --> 00:12:07,030
♪Now only fading warmth
remains in my palm♪

235
00:12:07,030 --> 00:12:09,950
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

236
00:12:10,390 --> 00:12:13,110
♪And paint a winter between your brows♪

237
00:12:13,110 --> 00:12:15,790
♪If we meet again in another life♪

238
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:18,830
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

239
00:12:19,510 --> 00:12:21,790
♪Was when we first met?♪

240
00:12:23,070 --> 00:12:25,470
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

241
00:12:26,590 --> 00:12:28,350
♪Was when we met for the last time?♪
